{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeE3EBwroKWj5RfTnqknf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018xBf2NuY9ni7GRtHYYBqqy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='kernels/indexer.cu'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''// Grid shape. Every block pays for one 32 KiB stage of `q`, so the block count is a cost, not just a\n// parallelism knob: it is capped near one full occupancy wave (7 blocks/SM is what 33 KiB of shared\n// out of 228 KiB allows) and the rows are handed out grid-stride inside that. DSV4_IXTILE_BLK\n// overrides the total for a sweep.'''\nnew='''// Grid shape. Every block pays for one 32 KiB stage of `q`, so the block count is a cost, not just a\n// parallelism knob: it is capped near one full occupancy wave (7 blocks/SM is what 33 KiB of shared\n// out of 228 KiB allows) and the rows are handed out grid-stride inside that. DSV4_IXTILE_BLK\n// overrides the total for a sweep.\n//\n// This is the ONLY CUDA API call on any index_score launch path, and it is on the TILED path, which\n// the engine never takes (it needs H % 8 != 0 or d % 32 != 0, and the model is H=64 d=128). That\n// matters because `compressed_decode_step_indexer` is CUDA-graph captured: `ixgemm_launch` issues a\n// kernel launch and nothing else, so the shipped path is capture-safe by construction rather than\n// by testing. gate_indexer_graph / gate_compressed_graph are the tests anyway.'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s); print(\"ok\")\nPY\nsleep 1; grep -c \"^built\" evidence/decode_loop/build_1p5_gate.log","description":"Document capture-safety of shipped path"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":178792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo