{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeE45KuDDoTJKKwb2ftbD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll wait for the builds. Meanwhile, here's where the iteration stands:\n\n**Ladder item 1.5 — `index_score` as a GEMM + fused epilogue.** Implemented and gated; the engine A/B is next.\n\nTwo kernels were written, because the first one hit a wall worth recording:\n\n| impl | claim | S=6, T=3072 (ctx 12,288 at ratio 4) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IXS_WARP` (ships today) | — | 898.8 µs |\n| `IXS_TILED` (q→shared, kv[t]→registers, d templated) | **bit-identical to `IXS_WARP`** | 448.5 µs — **2.00×** |\n| `IXS_GEMM` (8×8 register-tiled, serial-k, shared-P epilogue) | **bit-identical to `IXS_SCALAR`** | 132.7 µs — **6.77×** |\n\nThe tiled kernel caps at 2× because bit-exactness *with the warp kernel* mandates its 5-step `__shfl_down_sync` tree, and SHFL retires at one warp-instruction per SM per clock — a ~200 µs floor at this shape no matter how the operands are staged. So I changed which kernel the claim is against: a register-tiled GEMM accumulates serially in `k`, which is exactly `index_score_kernel`'s order — the correctness-first reference `gate_units` checks against `ref/goldens`. The warp kernel was itself adopted (Finding 68) as a deviation *from* that reference behind the LOSSLESS gate; 1.5 spends it back.\n\n`tests/gate_index_score` PASSes: 1130 shapes, **21.77 M floats compared bitwise across both claims, 0 differing**, plus two fallback controls (`d=96` → TILED must refuse, GEMM must not; `H=12` → the reverse). It also prints the deviation the change spends against the shipped warp kernel, per input distribution.\n\nOne pre-existing breakage surfaced and is fixed: `scripts/build_gate.sh` died at `gate_units` (link line missing `kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu`), and because that is a bare `nvcc` under `set -e`, **none of the twelve gates below it had rebuilt either** — the exact failure mode the file's own \"THE OTHER EIGHT\" block was written to prevent, reappearing above the block it was written in. Seven more link lines had the same gap.\n\nStill to run: `scripts/ixgemm_ab_run.sh` (detached, in `detach_audit.sh`'s `PATTERNS`) — the in-situ engine gates, both arms of the tok/s sweep with tau, both arms of a dprof pair on the `i:score` mark, and the LOSSLESS gate with a same-arm control. I've written down in advance that the tok/s sweep is expected to be marginal (~3.6 % if the mark scales with the kernel, against a 3.5–5.7 % spread) and that the dprof pair is the instrument that can actually resolve it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":188295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":183},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57fd2cef-3da8-407a-9390-ae21068668b7","uuid":"718caba3-222f-48c6-97e6-b6a3743ec6cb","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:09:14.442Z","request_id":"req_011CeE45JSeV74EGPJCAd2pL"}
